  <h1 class="entry-title center-text">I'm a teapot.</h1>

  <p>
    You asked us to brew you a coffee, but this is a travel blog run by two people
    who have collectively consumed their body weight in tea across three continents.
    We are, regrettably, a <strong>teapot</strong> — short, stout, and contractually
    incapable of producing coffee.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is HTTP status code <strong>418</strong>, and yes, it is a real one. It was
    defined in <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2324/">RFC&nbsp;2324, the
    Hyper Text Coffee Pot Control Protocol</a>, originally as an April Fools' joke in
    1998 and now as a permanent monument to internet whimsy.
  </p>

  <p>
    So tip us over, pour us out, and head somewhere more caffeinated:
  </p>

